# King Assistant - Hotword POC

This branch implements a hotword Proof‑of‑Concept (POC) targeted to your itel S25 (Android 15).

Quick checklist to enable Porcupine:
1. Put keyword file under: app/src/main/assets/porcupine/<your_keyword.ppn>
2. In app/build.gradle set PORCUPINE_ENABLED to true (or use gradle properties/local.properties)
3. Add Porcupine dependency to app/build.gradle (check Picovoice docs for the exact artifact & version)
4. Add PORCUPINE_ACCESS_KEY to local.properties or as a BuildConfig via Gradle

Build & test (local):
1. ./gradlew assembleDebug
2. adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
3. adb shell am start -n com.shahrafuking.kingassistant/.ui.HotwordTestActivity
4. From UI: Init Engine -> then speak the keyword (or use WakewordService once implemented)
5. View logs: adb logcat | grep -E "Porcupine|HotwordEngine|Hotword"

Security notes:
- Do NOT commit API keys or keyword files in the repo.
- Porcupine is optional; keep PORCUPINE_ENABLED=false to remain buildable without the dependency.
